                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "great soundtrack, game looks great.\n\nbut...\nthe zoomed in view is too close so you cant really react to anything that's coming at you. the visual indicator of incoming items does not really help with the fact that most of them in the early stage (at least) are homing and are faster than you unless you boost.\n\nyou can use the lock-on (which zooms you out and muffles the movement as your locked onto the target) can help with seeing the projectiles, but you then have to quickly drop back in to close view (not lock-on) to be able to react to anything coming at you (at which point you cant see them again).\n\nmight just be me but the above makes it very hard, I've got to stage 2 but with the speed of the game, i didn't even know that until i'd died which was a few moments after getting there.\n\ndifficulty level is pretty brutal right off the bat. the player of the steam video (of this above) is a god in the game. my play did not look half as controlled / skilled and i lasted around 1 to 2 minutes ish per play.\n\nperhaps some game difficulty settings added.\n\nstill, for the price, worth the punt. and i plan to stick at it to try to get further / better.\n\n",
